// Copy to Config/Local.xcconfig and fill in the values. That copy is gitignored.
//
// Without it, POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN is undefined, Info.plist's $(POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN)
// resolves to nothing, and PostHogConfiguration.configure() trips its DEBUG
// assertionFailure on launch. The release workflow does not read this file — it passes
// both values to xcodebuild directly from the `production` environment.
//
// The project token is a publishable key and is safe in a client build; it is kept out
// of git so desktop, iOS and any future staging project cannot be confused for one
// another. See docs/analytics.md.
//
// The // in a URL would be parsed as an xcconfig comment, so break it with $().

// PostHog — "KeigoButton Desktop (macOS)", project 549465. NOT the iOS keyboard's
// token: mixing the two is the one thing docs/analytics.md exists to prevent.
POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN =
POSTHOG_HOST = https:/$()/us.i.posthog.com
